# Phone Projection Middleware - Adaptation Guide

## Overview

This document describes how to adapt the Generic Phone Projection Middleware to different automotive projection platforms. The middleware is designed with a clear separation between platform-agnostic core functionality and platform-specific adapters.

## Architecture Recap


┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    Application Layer                         │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                  Middleware Core (Platform-Agnostic)        │
│  ┌─────────────┐ ┌─────────────┐ ┌─────────────┐           │
│  │  Session    │ │  Lifecycle  │ │   Event     │           │
│  │  Manager    │ │  Manager    │ │  Router     │           │
│  └──────┬──────┘ └──────┬──────┘ └──────┬──────┘           │
│         │               │               │                   │
├─────────┼───────────────┼───────────────┼───────────────────┤
│         ▼               ▼               ▼                   │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │           IPlatformAdapter (Abstract Interface)      │   │
│  ├──────────┬──────────┬──────────┬──────────┬────────┤   │
│  │Connect...│Resource..│  Input   │   UI     │Capabili│   │
│  │  Mgr     │  Mgr     │ Handler  │ Renderer │ty Provider│  │
│  └──────────┴──────────┴──────────┴──────────┴────────┘   │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
         │               │               │               │
         ▼               ▼               ▼               ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              Platform Adapter Implementations                │
│  ┌──────────────┐ ┌──────────────┐ ┌──────────────┐         │
│  │ Android Auto │ │  CarPlay*    │ │ Proprietary  │         │
│  │   Adapter    │ │  (Future)    │ │   Adapter    │         │
│  └──────────────┘ └──────────────┘ └──────────────┘         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

CarPlay: is an additional future platform adapter which is not included in this PoC
=====================================================================================================
New Platform Adapter

1. Define a new class that derives from ‘PlatformAdapterBase’:

// include/my_platform/my_platform_adapter.hpp
#include "platform/platform_adapter.hpp"

namespace phone_projection {
namespace my_platform {

class MyPlatformAdapter : public platform::PlatformAdapterBase {
public:
MyPlatformAdapter() {
metadata_.name = "my_platform";
metadata_.version = "1.0.0";
metadata_.description = "My Platform Projection Adapter";
metadata_.supported_transports = {"usb", "wifi"};

// Define platform capabilities
capabilities_.supports_touch = true;
capabilities_.supports_rotary = false;
// ... etc

// Create component implementations
connection_manager_ = std::make_unique();
resource_manager_ = std::make_unique();
input_handler_ = std::make_unique();
ui_renderer_ = std::make_unique();
capability_provider_ = std::make_unique();
}

Result initialize(const std::string& config) override {
// Parse config, initialize platform SDK
return Result();
}

Result shutdown() override {
// Cleanup platform SDK
return Result();
}
};
} // namespace my_platform
} // namespace phone_projection

// Register the adapter
REGISTER_ADAPTER(phone_projection::my_platform::MyPlatformAdapter, my_platform)

2. Define component interfaces
Every component should also define one or more interfaces:
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Connection Manager (IConnectionManager)

class MyConnectionManager : public platform::ConnectionManagerBase {
public:
Result connect(const VehicleProfile& profile) override {
// 1. Initialize transport (USB/WiFi/Bluetooth)
// 2. Perform platform-specific handshake
// 3. Start data receive loop
// 4. Update state to Connected
return Result();
}

Result disconnect() override {
// 1. Stop data receive loop
// 2. Send disconnect notification
// 3. Close transport
// 4. Update state to Disconnected
return Result();
}

Result send_data(const std::vector& data) override {
// Serialize and send via transport
return Result();
}
};

Responsibilities:
-Initialisation of transport protocols (USB, Bluetooth, WiFi etc);
-Handshaking;
-Packet assembly and dis-assembly;
-Tracking of connection status;
-Re-connection.
*********************************************************************

Resource Manager (IResourceManager)

class MyResourceManager : public platform::ResourceManagerBase {
public:
Result request_resource(ResourceType type,
const std::string& session_id) override {
// Platform-specific resource acquisition
// e.g., Audio focus via platform audio policy
//       Video surface via platform compositor
return ResourceManagerBase::request_resource(type, session_id);
}
}

Responsibilities include:
- Audio ducking, pause and play.
- Video composition and resizing.
- Keyboard, rotary and touch input focus.
- Navigational turn-by-turn focus.
*********************************************************************
Input Handler (IInputHandler)
class MyInputHandler : public platform::InputHandlerBase {
public:
Result send_input(const Event& event) override {

// Translate middleware event to platform format
switch (event.type) {
case EventType::TouchDown:
case EventType::TouchUp:
case EventType::TouchMove:
send_touch_event(static_cast(event));
break;
case EventType::RotaryClockwise:
case EventType::RotaryCounterClockwise:
send_rotary_event(static_cast(event));
break;
// ... etc
}
return Result();
}
Result set_focus(bool focused) override {
// Notify platform of focus change
return Result();
}
};
Responsibilities are:
- Conversion of middle-ware input events into platform events.
- Input focus management.
- Platform specific input delivery.
- Specification of input types supported.
*********************************************************************
UI renderer (IUiRenderer)
class MyUiRenderer : public platform::UiRendererBase {
public:
Result render_template(TemplateType type,
const std::string& json_payload) override {
// Convert template to platform format
// e.g., Android Auto: Car App Library templates
//       CarPlay: CarPlay UI templates
//       Custom: Proprietary layout system
return Result();
}
};
Responsibilities include:
- Template mapping.
- Surface management.
- Renderer integration.
- Responsive layout.
*********************************************************************
Capability Provider (ICapabilityProvider)
class MyCapabilityProvider : public platform::CapabilityProviderBase {
public:
MyCapabilityProvider() {
capabilities_.supports_touch = true;
capabilities_.supports_rotary = false;
capabilities_.supports_voice = true;
// ... define all capabilities
capabilities_.supported_codecs = {"H264", "VP9"};
capabilities_.supported_templates = {"MediaTemplate", "ListTemplate", "NavTemplate"};
}
};
Responsibilities include:
- Specification of platform capabilities.
- Capability negotiation.
- Checking of version compatibility.
*********************************************************************
*********************************************************************
3. Build
In src/my_platform/CMakeLists.txt, add:

add_library(pp_my_platform STATIC
my_platform_adapter.cpp
my_connection_manager.cpp
my_resource_manager.cpp
my_input_handler.cpp
my_ui_renderer.cpp
my_capability_provider.cpp
)
*********************************************************************
target_include_directories(pp_my_platform
PUBLIC
$
PRIVATE
${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}
)
target_link_libraries(pp_my_platform
PUBLIC
pp_common
pp_platform
pp_core
)
*********************************************************************
# Add to main build
# In src/CMakeLists.txt:
# add_subdirectory(my_platform)
