*********************************************************************
## Platform-Specific Considerations
### Android Auto (Reference Implementation - This PoC)
| Aspect | Implementation Detail |
|--------|----------------------|
| Transport | USB (ADB-like) or Bluetooth (PAN) |
| Protocol | Proprietary binary protocol over transport |
| UI Model | Car App Library (template-based) |
| Audio | Media session + audio focus |
| Video | SurfaceTexture/SurfaceView composition |
| Input | Rotary, touch, keyboard, voice |
| Safety | Driver distraction API (UX restrictions) |
*********************************************************************
*********************************************************************
### Apple CarPlay (Future Extension)(will not bein demo app)
| Aspect | Implementation Detail |
|--------|----------------------|
| Transport | USB (iAP2) or WiFi (Bonjour + TLS) |
| Protocol | iAP2 over transport, CarPlay protocol |
| UI Model | CarPlay templates (similar but different) |
| Audio | CoreAudio + audio session |
| Video | IOSurface / CoreVideo |
| Input | Touch, rotary (via HID), Siri |
| Security | Certificate-based authentication |
*********************************************************************
*********************************************************************
### Proprietary IVI Systems (Future Extension) (Working .... in progress)
| Aspect | Implementation Detail |
|--------|----------------------|
| Transport | Vendor-specific (Ethernet, CAN, ) |
| Protocol | Vendor-defined (looking for working expl..in progress) |
| UI Model | Custom (Qt, native, HTML, currently a console based) |
| Audio | Vendor audio framework (PCM, currently a console based) |
| Video | Vendor compositor ( currently a console based) |
| Input | Vendor input system (libinput, currently a console based) |
*********************************************************************
*********************************************************************
### Smart Cluster / Instrument Cluster (Working .... in progress 80% implemented)
| Aspect | Implementation Detail |
|--------|----------------------|
| Transport | CAN, Ethernet  |
| Protocol | ASAM XCP, SOME/IP, can be vendor-specific |
| UI Model |  gauges, minimal templates |
| Safety | Demo, so not checking  |
| Latency | < 50ms, will check is future after demo is accepted |
| Priority | Safety-critical path |
*********************************************************************
*********************************************************************
## Configuration for New Platforms
Add platform configuration to JSON config:
{
"platform_configs": {
"my_platform": {
"transport": "usb",
"vendor_id": "0x1234",
"product_id": "0x5678",
"firmware_version": "2.0.0",
"enable_feature_x": "true",
"custom_parameter": "value"
}
}
}
*********************************************************************
Adapter interface
Result MyPlatformAdapter::initialize(const std::string& config)
{
nlohmann::json json = nlohmann::json::parse(config);
std::string transport = json.value("transport", "usb");
}
*********************************************************************
New adapters

Unit tests (smart cluster)
// tests/test_my_platform_adapter.cpp
#include
#include "my_platform/my_platform_adapter.hpp"
TEST(MyPlatformAdapterTest, Initialise)
{
std::unique_ptr adapter = std::make_unique();
Result result = adapter->initialize("{}");
EXPECT_TRUE(result.is_ok());
}
TEST(MyPlatformAdapterTest, Connect/Disconnect)
{
std::unique_ptr adapter = std::make_unique();
adapter->initialize("{}");

VehicleProfile profile = create_test_profile();
Result conn_result = adapter->get_connection_manager()->connect(profile);
EXPECT_TRUE(conn_result.is_ok());
// Wait for connection
Result disc_result = adapter->get_connection_manager()->disconnect();
EXPECT_TRUE(disc_result.is_ok());
}
*********************************************************************
Integration tests
// tests/integration/test_my_platform_integration.cpp
TEST(MyPlatformIntegration, End-to-end)
{
std::unique_ptr middleware = create_projection_middleware();
middleware->lifecycle_manager()->load_adapter("my_platform");
middleware->lifecycle_manager()->set_active_adapter("my_platform");
VehicleProfile profile = create_test_profile();
Result session = middleware->create_and_connect_session(profile);
EXPECT_TRUE(session.is_ok());
// Test resource requests
Result audio = middleware->session_manager()->request_audio_focus(session.value());
EXPECT_TRUE(audio.is_ok());
// Test input injection

middleware->session_manager()->disconnect(session.value());
}
*********************************************************************
Migration tasks
To migrate to a new platform you need to:
[ ] Create a capability matrix
[ ] Develop an IConnectionManager (transport and protocol functionality)
[ ] Develop an IResourceManager (audio, video, input and nav functionality)
[ ] Develop an IInputHandler (mapping of events)
[ ] Develop an IUiRenderer (mapping of templates)
[ ] Develop an ICapabilityProvider (declaration of capabilities)
[ ] Subclass PlatformAdapterBase
[ ] Register using REGISTER_ADAPTER
[ ] Configure CMake build
[ ] Develop unit tests
[ ] Develop integration tests
[ ] Note platform specific requirements
[ ] Include sample vehicle profile
*********************************************************************

Common approaches
•Asynchronous processing
•Leverage the event router to handle asynchronous processing:
•Within connection manager
•void on_protocol_handshake_complete() {
•set_state(State::Connected);
// Notify middleware
if (data_callback_) {
std::vector connected_msg = {0x01, 0x00}; // Connected
notify_data_received(connected_msg);
}
}
*********************************************************************
Error Handling
Result MyConnectionManager::connect(const VehicleProfile& profile)
{
if (!transport_->open()) {
set_state(State::Error, core::ErrorCode::ConnectionFailed);
return Result(core::make_error_code(core::ErrorCode::ConnectionFailed));
}
}
*********************************************************************
Conclusion

Using the middleware’s adapter pattern means that new projection platforms can be added without having to change central functions. Adapters provide a clean interface to hide platform specific implementation details. Benefits include:
1. Separation – platform issues are contained so do not impact on central functions

2. Testability – adapters can be replaced with mocks or stubs
3. Separation – clear division between areas of concern
4. Scalability – simply add new adapters for additional platforms
5. Customisation – vehicle profiles are used to negotiate capabilities

